{
  "title": "Cache the prompt prefix across turns of the edit tool loop",
  "description": "The Edit with AI tool loop (ramekin-core/src/ai/edit_recipe.rs run_edit_loop) resends the whole conversation every turn: the system prompt (house_style's embeds all of doc/house-style.md, about 1.2k tokens), the recipe, and every earlier tool reply. \
Nothing in ramekin-core/src/ai sets `cache_control`, and Anthropic models on OpenRouter only cache prompts when asked, so every turn bills the full prefix at full input price; input grows roughly quadratically with the turn count. \
This used to matter only for manual Edit with AI runs, but the house_style normalize op now runs the loop on every import, on the edit model (Opus): the first eval run cost about $0.20 per recipe (data/ai-evals/house-style.md). \
Add a cache breakpoint (OpenRouter's `cache_control: {type: ephemeral}` on the last content part of the system message and/or the latest message) to ChatRequest/ChatMessage for tool-loop requests, keeping our own disk cache keys stable. \
Check the saving with a house-style eval rerun on fresh cache (the 'Cost of accepted calls' column).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
